      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That sense of being rendered obsolete or broken because your old mission is over is a very specific type of pain that doesn't always fit the standard label for depression. It speaks to a deep questioning of purpose when the external reasons for living are stripped away, which is incredibly heavy but also a natural part of growth when one's story fundamentally shifts. Please know that even when it feels like there is no utility left in you, your existence still holds value beyond any role or function you once played.",
      "source": "target",
